Equation of tangent at $(4,2)$ is

\begin{aligned}
& y y_1=\frac{1}{2}\left(x+x_1\right) \\
& \Rightarrow 2 y=\frac{1}{2}(x+2) \Rightarrow 4 y=x+2 \\
& \Rightarrow y=\frac{x}{4}+\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}

So, slope of tangent $=\frac{1}{4}\therefore$ Slope of normal $=-4$
